Screenshots are off for the first four commits of Phase 6.

Those four are packages/core, packages/db, a migration and a worker job. None of
them imports a component, renders a page or changes a stylesheet, so every
baseline in tests/visual/__screenshots__ is a photograph of markup they cannot
reach. Running Playwright over them costs a build and two viewports per commit
to prove nothing moved.

Until: the first commit that touches apps/web, which is Configuration > Lead
Sources. That commit deletes this file, and the screenshots come back on with
four new pages to record.

This is not a licence to skip the rest of the gate. typecheck, lint, build and
the whole test suite still run on every one of those commits - `verify:no-visual`
drops exactly one stage.
